# One line ending everywhere. Git for Windows checks CRLF out by default, which
# is not a cosmetic difference here: dprint reports every checkout file as
# "Text differed by line endings" on the Windows CI job, and tests that compare
# file text see the same drift. `text=auto` keeps binary detection; `eol=lf`
# pins the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff, never merge.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary

# API Extractor writes its reports with CRLF. Keep the bytes it produces: a
# checkout that normalises them to LF makes `api:check` see a spurious diff.
**/etc/*.api.md -text
